 ### [Work-Efficient Scan](10349-work-efficient-scan.md)
-A parallel algorithm to compute the inclusive prefix sum of an array using a two-phase approach (upsweep/reduction and downsweep) to achieve work efficiency ($O(n)$ work, $O(\log n)$ depth). It builds on [Naive Parallel Prefix Sum (Scan)](10348-naive-parallel-prefix-sum-scan.md) by replacing the iterative $O(n \log n)$ work with a binary tree reduction, eliminating race conditions through in-place updates and synchronization. It is distinguished from the naive method by its tree-based structure and from hardware-optimized variants by its explicit multi-kernel orchestration for arbitrary input sizes.
+A parallel algorithm to compute the inclusive prefix sum of an array using a two-phase approach (upsweep/reduction and downsweep) to achieve work efficiency ($O(n)$ work, $O(\log n)$ depth). It builds on [Naive Parallel Prefix Sum (Scan)](10348-naive-parallel-prefix-sum-scan.md) by replacing the iterative $O(n \log n)$ work with a binary tree reduction, eliminating race conditions through in-place updates and synchronization.
 
 ### Naive GPU Parallel Scan
 A naive GPU-based parallel scan implementation, implemented in the `StreamCompaction::Naive` namespace [S2, unofficial].
+
+### 4-way Prefix Sum
+A parallel prefix sum algorithm that concurrently generates binary masks for each radix combination, computes local prefix sums, merges results, and outputs total counts per block [S4, unofficial]. It generates binary masks for each radix combination, computes the local prefix sum of the mask, merges the prefix sum results for all combinations, and sends the total number of each radix combination in each block to the output block sum array [S4, unofficial].
 
